write('BUG_REPORT.md','# Bug report\n\nThis audit did not push or deploy code. Concurrent owner changes and commits were preserved. Fixed means a local code change with the stated regression evidence, not a production repair.\n\n'+''.join(f'## {id}: {severity} — {state}\n\n{desc}\n\nEvidence: {evidence}.\n\n' for id,severity,state,desc,evidence in bugs)+'## Test infrastructure incident\n\nOne regression run overlapped another schema-reset test run and produced missing-table failures. It is retained as integration-final.json and receives no passing credit. The clean run uses a separately named watcon_regression_test database and is integration-verified.json. The original development cluster remained in recovery; the audit used a fresh separate cluster without deleting its files. Windows browser-server teardown required stopping only the known audit Next process after all 9 tests completed; the browser JSON records that waiting time.\n')

security='# Security audit update 24 November 2026\n\nScope: source review, real local PostgreSQL tests, production Super Admin read-only navigation, signed-out API probes. This is not a penetration-test certification. No authentication bypass or production transaction was attempted.\n\n'
security+='## Verified controls\n\n- Argon2 password hashing and database-backed, hashed opaque session tokens. HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax cookies; secure in production. Idle and absolute expiry, logout and deactivation have local tests.\n- Password reset tokens are single-use; reset revokes sessions. Generic authentication errors and account/IP limits have local tests. Mailbox delivery remains blocked.\n- Organization/project scopes are applied by services. All nine role defaults exist; individual local page probes and service authorization tests do not prove the entire role-by-action matrix.\n- Attachment bytes use PostgreSQL attachment_blobs by default; filesystem is an alternative. Access follows the owning resource; hashes are checked before serving bytes. Version and evidence-retention controls are tested.\n- Fixed metadata exposure and malformed-origin handling locally. Direct anonymous document endpoints return 401 in production.\n- State changes use Server Actions with framework origin checks; upload handler also checks origin/host. Reverse-proxy trust configuration requires deployment review.\n- SQL inputs normally use Prisma and tagged parameterized SQL. No dynamic untrusted SQL exploitation was demonstrated. The one reviewed dangerouslySetInnerHTML script is a fixed root-layout constant; this is not blanket XSS clearance.\n- Security headers exist and are sampled on the deployed health response. A full app CSP is not configured.\n\n## Remaining risks and configuration\n\n'
security+='- Dependency audit: '+str(deps.get('metadata',{}).get('vulnerabilities',{}))+'. Entries include transitive chains; eight package entries do not mean eight independent root vulnerabilities. Review runtime reachability and patched upstream releases before release.\n- XLSX signature/extension checks and CSV NUL checks are not full content validation. No malware scanner is integrated or tested. Upload body buffering and platform limits need a capacity test.\n- Database least-privilege grants, provider firewall policy, encryption configuration, backup retention and restore ability were not independently inspected. Do not assume Supabase RLS replaces app authorization; the actual app uses direct PostgreSQL via Prisma.\n- Test database reset scripts guard database-name suffixes; run only against explicitly provisioned isolated targets. The new audit cluster uses local port 5544.\n- No raw .env values, credentials, session tokens or real business records are included in these reports. Tracked-file inspection found only .env.example among environment files; this is not a full historical secret scan.\n- Production credentials for roles other than Super Admin were not supplied.\n\n## Release requirements\n\nResolve or formally assess the high dependency chain; review default grants against real departments; test protected document metadata after deploying to staging; validate SMTP with a test mailbox; perform a backup restore drill. No migrations or changes were made to production.\n'
write('SECURITY_AUDIT.md',security)

training=data('training/reconciliation.json',{})
write('FINANCIAL_RECONCILIATION.md','# Financial reconciliation\n\nLocal fictional training scenario passed through real service logic and real PostgreSQL. Evidence: training-test.json and training/reconciliation.json. Six PDFs were built from saved training documents. The clean full suite also repeats the scenario.\n\nPurchase: 10 × ₹1,000 = ₹10,000 taxable; CGST ₹900 + SGST ₹900 = ₹1,800; approved bill ₹11,800. Two payments ₹5,000 and ₹6,800 fully allocated; payable ₹0.\n\nSales: 10 × ₹1,500 = ₹15,000 taxable; GST ₹2,700; certified RA → issued invoice ₹17,700. Receipts ₹7,080 + ₹10,620 allocated; receivable ₹0. Contract value stays ₹17,700 because the linked SO is not counted a second time. Material cost ₹10,000; material margin ₹5,000 (33.33%). No labour, overheads, retention, recovery or TDS in this simple example. RA eligibility currently follows contract quantities and certification, not a mandatory delivery-challan link; this business-rule gap needs an owner decision. Separate suites test TDS, partial allocation, credits and reversals.\n\nProject Accounts billed amounts come from issued client invoices, not RA claims. Amount received includes posted project receipts and client TDS; receivable is net invoice due less allocated receipts and notes. Unallocated advances are different from invoice settlement. Supplier payable is approved net bill amount less allocated payments/notes. Do not infer net receivables from cash alone.\n\nMoney uses decimal-scaled integer helpers and PostgreSQL Decimal storage. Intra/inter-state tax and rounding assertions passed locally. This is application arithmetic verification, not statutory GST advice.\n\nProduction reconciliation: BLOCKED. Obtain a read-only transaction export with statuses, allocations, credits, cancellations and project links. Compare per-document lines and tax, then reconcile party ledgers, project totals and dashboard figures. Never repair a difference with an unexplained adjustment.\n\nUnimplemented/limited: operational sub-ledger, no verified general-ledger close or complete expense-inclusive project profit. The former 1000-project truncation has been removed and a 1003-project regression passed; large-portfolio load testing remains open.\n')
write('INVENTORY_RECONCILIATION.md','# Inventory reconciliation\n\nConfirmed implemented rule: supplier GRN posting adds accepted stock. Supplier bill approval does not add stock. This differs from the requested supplier-bill stock trigger and requires a business-owner decision before any rule change.\n\nABC Hotel test: new filter/brand has zero opening stock; PO approval leaves zero; supplier receipts of 6 and 4 posted to Central Warehouse yield 10; approved supplier bill leaves 10; SO approval leaves 10; client deliveries of 4 and 6 leave zero. The saved balance and financial cost match the expected values. Evidence: complete-training-workflow.test.ts, training-test.json, training/reconciliation.json.\n\nOther local integration tests cover independent item/brand balances, location totals, reservations, simultaneous outward movement, retry idempotency, future/backdated movements, internal transit receipts, discrepancy write-offs, returns and reversals. The ledger engine locks balance rows and posts through a deterministic unique idempotency key inside the document transaction.\n\nAn internal transfer dispatch moves stock from source to transit. Destination receipt moves transit to destination. Supplier receipt increases company stock; an internal receipt must not be counted as another purchase. Damaged/rejected supplier quantities do not become accepted stock.\n\nProduction accuracy: BLOCKED. No read-only production stock/ledger export was supplied. Reconcile each item-brand-location balance to signed ledger movements; sum locations to company quantities; compare GRN accepted counters, PO pending quantities, reservations and challan transit. Investigate every mismatch before an authorized adjustment with a reason. No production count was changed.\n')

scoretext='\n'.join(f'- {k}: {v["score"]}% ({v["passed"]}/{v["applicable"]} credited checks).' for k,v in scores.items())
write('PRODUCTION_READINESS.md',f'# Production readiness\n\nVerdict: **NO-GO** for declaring the complete ERP production-ready. Existing production was not changed, pushed or deployed.\n\nEvidence readiness score: {overall}%. This is the arithmetic mean of eight category scores; each is passed applicable checks / all applicable checks × 100. Failed, blocked and unexecuted checks receive zero. It is a conservative evidence score, not the probability that the app is correct, not branch coverage and not certification. Render checks have narrow expected results. Reclassifying or expanding the checklist changes the score.\n\n{scoretext}\n\n## Release blockers\n\n1. Decide and sign off the stock-posting rule (currently GRN). Keep one physical posting per receipt.\n2. Review the high dependency chain with a patched supported version or a documented reachability assessment; rerun audit/build/regressions.\n3. Reconcile production bills, receipts, inventory and dashboards using authorized read-only exports.\n4. Prove SMTP password reset and a managed-database backup restore in isolation.\n5. Execute remaining commercial UI flows, all role/action/API combinations, offline/save recovery, cross-browser and load checks in staging.\n6. Review the new help/manual downloads and screenshots in the final staging build; Word rendering status is stated in COMPLETE_APP_AUDIT.md.\n\n## Safe next steps\n\nReview local git diff. Start scripts/audit-db.mjs to create the isolated local cluster. Set TEST_DATABASE_URL to the dedicated local regression database for integration tests. Do not use a real organization database. Build and run the application against an isolated target, repeat the checklist, then obtain owner approval for deployment. Never run test resets, demo seeding or bootstrap against production.\n')
write('COMPLETE_APP_AUDIT.md',f'# WATCON Enterprise complete application audit\n\nAudit date: 24 November 2026, Asia/Kolkata. Main application: WATCON-APP. Live application: https://watcon-app.vercel.app/. Verdict: **NO-GO** for full ERP production-readiness certification.\n\n## Scope and measured totals\n\n- User-facing modules: {len(modules)+2}, including Authentication and the new Help & User Guide.\n- Exported module operations discovered: {len(features)} (includes helper operations; exact inventory in FEATURE_INVENTORY.csv).\n- Page/handler route files: {len(routes)}. Prisma models: {len(models)}.\n- Test cases in this audit ledger: {len(cases)}. Passed {counts["passed"]}; failed {counts["failed"]}; blocked {counts["blocked"]}; not executed {counts["not executed"]}.\n- Tracked findings: {len(bugs)}. Fixed locally: 8. Remaining or decision-required: {len(bugs)-8}. Dependency findings are package entries and can share a root advisory.\n- Evidence readiness score: {overall}%, equal mean of the eight scored categories below.\n\n{scoretext}\n\n## Architecture and relationships\n\nNext.js 16.4.6 App Router, React 19.3, TypeScript, Tailwind/Radix UI, Prisma 7.10 and PostgreSQL via pg adapter. Local PostgreSQL is embedded; production connection/provider settings were not independently inspected. The app is not Firebase-backed. Attachments default to transactionally stored PostgreSQL blobs; filesystem is an alternate driver. PDFs use @react-pdf/renderer, bundled Noto fonts and WATCON logo.\n\nOrganizations scope users, projects, parties, item/brands and documents. Projects link members and tasks; tasks have many assignees/departments. Supplier flow links planning/requisitions, enquiries/quotations, PO lines, GRN lines, matched supplier bills and payment allocations. Client flow links Client PO lines, Sales Order lines, challans, RA certification, issued invoices and receipts. Stock transactions and location balances track physical events. Audit logs and document revisions retain history. See DATABASE_SCHEMA_INVENTORY.md and ROUTE_INVENTORY.csv for the exhaustive generated inventory.\n\n## Verified results and limits\n\nThe clean local unit/integration results are unit-final.json and integration-verified.json. The current Phase 1 Chromium workflow is e2e-current.json. The actual standalone help/manual and optimized-logo smoke checks are built-help.json. Source-level checks and old reports are not substitutes for runtime evidence. Earlier failed harness runs are retained and are not counted as passing results. Testcase granularity varies: one service test can assert multiple transitions; a route smoke check proves only rendering.\n\nProduction: authorized Super Admin login and logout, 28 read-only module route GETs, blank PO/SO form inspection, sampled desktop/tablet/mobile geometry and signed-out document API checks. No fictional business transaction was sent to production. No private production data was captured into the manuals. Live screenshots are sign-in only.\n\nLocal: isolated PostgreSQL clusters/databases, real migrations, service regressions, project/task browser workflow, commercial training chain, stock concurrency, PDF fixtures, role probes and screenshot/UI results as recorded in the evidence files. Financial and inventory production balances remain unverified. The separate commercial UI chain in procurement-ui.json created and approved a PO, posted a receipt, approved and paid its supplier bill, approved an SO, dispatched a client challan, issued the client invoice and allocated the receipt; persisted amounts and stock were cross-checked.\n\nThe ABC Hotel chain verifies partial receipts and deliveries, bill approval without double stock, linked CPO/SO contract accounting, RA certification, invoice issue and partial two-sided settlements. It uses fictional values and does not claim every procurement/UI/closure branch was exercised. RFQ award and project/task workflows have separate tests.\n\n## UI and employee guidance\n\nThe new /help route uses the existing theme, searchable articles, tutorials, glossary, FAQs, troubleshooting, guidance for each operational role and Super-Admin-only manual downloads. At the owner request, access is through Administration > Help & guide; the general sidebar and contextual links have been removed. No business records are embedded in the help content.\n\nThe current UI provides draft/approval/posting distinctions and inline validation, but employees need explicit training on GRN versus supplier bill, transit versus available site stock, RA versus tax invoice, and allocated payments versus advances. Source labels and fictional UI captures underpin the manual; a source-backed instruction does not imply an executed UI workflow.\n\nMobile usability: sampled route/form geometry only; full real-device accessibility and every-page form validation are not certified. Performance: local tests and request timings, no fresh load benchmark; development compilation times are not production response measurements.\n\n## Documents and PDF status\n\nRequested Markdown, PDF, DOCX and Quick Start files are generated in docs/user-guide. Screenshots are under its screenshots folder. PDFs have cover, contents, logo, page numbering, simple workflow diagrams and local screenshots where available. PDF geometry tests and text-bounds inspection passed; visual sampling does not prove all unseen data combinations. Word-render limitations are recorded in evidence/WORD_RENDER_LIMITATION.md; if no word-manual-render.pdf exists, the DOCX layout remains blocked despite the generated OOXML.\n\n## Unverified areas and exact follow-up\n\nRead PRODUCTION_READINESS.md and the blocked/unexecuted rows of TEST_CASES.csv. Obtain authorized read-only DB exports and deployment logs; supply test mailbox and backups; use isolated staging to finish the commercial UI/role/device/load matrix. Resolve the stock-rule decision and dependency risks before a deployment review. This audit performed no push, deployment or destructive production migration. Concurrent owner edits were preserved and final access checks reflect the requested Super-Admin-only help policy.\n\n## Reproducibility\n\nReport generator: scripts/build-audit-reports.py. Manual/content generators: scripts/build-help-content.py and scripts/build-user-manuals.py. Local UI runner: scripts/audit-ui.mjs (hardcoded localhost:3200 and the fictional training fixture only). PDF QA: scripts/audit-artifact-qa.py. Raw outputs are in docs/audit/evidence. Do not publish development server logs or test fixtures as real business data.\n')
print(json.dumps({'modules':len(modules)+2,'operations':len(features),'routes':len(routes),'models':len(models),'cases':len(cases),'counts':counts,'scores':scores,'readiness':overall},indent=2))
